      "estimand": "The causal effect of an increase in adherence to a suppression‑conditional recommended defensive mix (per one standard‑deviation of the adherence score) on the probability of winning a game, holding constant team and opponent strength, venue, and schedule factors.",
      "unit": "Game (one team‑observation per game). Each observation is a team‑game, with the adherence metric computed from that team’s defensive possessions in that game.",
      "sample": "All regular‑season and playoff games from the 2022‑23 through 2025‑26 seasons (approximately 5,000–6,000 team‑games). Games used to train the suppression recommendation model are strictly held-out (sliding‑window design: train on seasons i−1 and earlier, predict on season i). Garbage‑time possessions (final 2 minutes with lead ≥15) are excluded.",
      "power": "With N ≈ 5,000 and an assumed small effect size (odds ratio ≈ 1.05 per SD increase in adherence), a logistic regression with controls for team and opponent fixed effects will have >80% power at α = 0.05 two‑sided. This improves dramatically over a series‑level test.",
      "controls": "Team defensive fixed effects (overall defensive quality), opponent offensive fixed effects, indicator for home/away, days of rest, back‑to‑back indicator, and a pre‑game win‑probability proxy (e.g., betting market implied odds or pre‑game team Elo rating).",
      "falsification": "1) Shuffle adherence scores across games within teams; if the original signal persists, it is spurious. 2) Replace the suppression‑conditional recommendation with a placebo recommendation (e.g., a random or static strategy mix) and verify no predictive power. 3) Limit analysis to first‑half adherence predicting full‑game win to rule out reverse causality from score effects.",
      "multiplicity": "Pre‑register a single primary adherence metric (e.g., proportion of possessions where the actual coverage matches the model’s top‑1 recommendation for that suppression context). All secondary definitions (top‑2, weighted match) are explicitly labeled as exploratory and subjected to Holm‑Bonferroni correction.",
      "decision_rule": "Report the adjusted odds ratio and its 95% CI from a mixed‑effects logistic regression (random intercepts for team and opponent) or a conditional logit with clustered standard errors. If the two‑sided p‑value is below 0.05, conclude adherence predicts winning; otherwise conclude no reliable effect at game level. Full model specification, diagnostics, and a sensitivity analysis for unmeasured confounding (E‑value) will be reported.",
      "data_version": "NBA per‑game files from the NBA stats API (play‑by‑play with action type/sub‑type, clock, period, score, player, shot distance/result; substitution intervals; starters; defensive matchup minutes) and derived play‑type possession records from the graph database, covering 2022‑23 through 2025‑26 as committed on 2026‑04‑13."
    }
  }
}

